WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.880
There's nothing quite like a good kiss to break&nbsp;
a heart or two — as fans of these shows will tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.600
you. Whether it's a tragic farewell, a shocking&nbsp;
betrayal, or even a chance to save a life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.520
each kiss easily ranks among the greatest&nbsp;
tear-jerking moments in TV history.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.800
Few shows manage to throw more tragic obstacles&nbsp;
between a couple than The Good Place. Heck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.800
the fact that Eleanor and Chidi's relationship&nbsp;
survives past that horrifying clown bed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.760
begin with is a testament to their deep bond. But&nbsp;
through reboot after reboot, the pair continually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:32.800
finds their way back to each other, giving fans&nbsp;
some hope that true love does, in fact, endure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.640
Sadly, all good things must come to an&nbsp;
end — at least for a while, that is.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.160
By the later seasons of The Good Place,&nbsp;
Eleanor and Chidi just aren't themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.400
unless they're sacrificing their happiness to&nbsp;
save not only the world, but the afterlife too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.600
So it only fits that the season 3&nbsp;
finale sees the pair wipe Chidi's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.200
memory to save the Good Place, and&nbsp;
the souls of all humanity, for good.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.400
As if that weren't enough to tug at&nbsp;
the heartstrings, demon-turned-good-guy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:58.320
Michael sets up a "greatest hits" montage&nbsp;
of Chidi and Eleanore's moments throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.920
their hundreds of reboots. Of course,&nbsp;
Eleanor can't help lighten the mood…

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.560
"I know you're deflecting by making&nbsp;
jokes about how hot you are."

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.120
"It's not a joke, I'm a legit snack."

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:12.320
...But there are tears all around when she kisses&nbsp;
Chidi, and the season, goodbye. The brutal blow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:16.320
of this not-so-final kiss between Eleanor and&nbsp;
Chidi is only softened by the knowledge that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.480
in the end, these two get the happy ending&nbsp;
they deserve — however bittersweet it may be.

00:01:22.025 --> 00:01:24.720
Supernatural's Dean and Jo had a will&nbsp;
they/won't they vibe from the moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.640
she showed up in season 2, but Dean was&nbsp;
careful not to cross the line. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:33.120
Dean's self-restraint gets thrown out the window&nbsp;
in "Abandon All Hope" when the apocalypse comes…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.280
again. And for the first time ever, Dean&nbsp;
tries unsuccessfully to pick someone up.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.520
"Sweetheart, if this is our last night on Earth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:43.040
I'm gonna spend it with a little&nbsp;
thing I call self-respect."

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:48.240
Clearly surprised at being rebuffed, Dean finally&nbsp;
sees Jo as an equal and a genuine potential match.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:53.120
Sadly, hell hath no fury like a Hellhound scorned.&nbsp;
While the hunter's brigade attempts to kill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:58.160
Lucifer, Jo's guts end up as puppy chow. Knowing&nbsp;
she's on death's door, she decides to sacrifice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:02.480
herself in a supernaturally charged blast to&nbsp;
give the Winchesters an open shot at Lucifer.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:06.560
With regret and grief in his eyes, Dean&nbsp;
kisses Jo on the forehead — but it isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.000
enough. Teasing what their relationship&nbsp;
could have been, he passionately kisses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.840
her before tearing himself away to have a&nbsp;
few words with the devil. The kicker? All&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:18.480
that sacrifice is for naught. Not even Samuel&nbsp;
Colt's gun can take out the root of all evil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.320
and Jo and her mother, Ellen, die in&nbsp;
vain. Talk about a cruel farewell.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.640
Criminal Minds isn't known for killing&nbsp;
off its main characters too often,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.800
but the death of Hotch's wife Haley was one of&nbsp;
the most shocking moments in the show's history.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:34.560
And while fans love to hate the episode, it's&nbsp;
hard to argue that it isn't one of the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.880
brilliant of the whole series. Chilling&nbsp;
and gut-wrenching, sure. But brilliant.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.360
Later, as Hotch is fighting for&nbsp;
his own life in the hospital,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:45.200
he meets up with Hailey in a trance-like&nbsp;
vision. They watch her son's home videos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.560
at a theater — an apparent homage to&nbsp;
watching over someone after death.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:54.000
Haley then convinces him to move on and be&nbsp;
happy — because it just isn't his time to die.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.520
After years of tormenting himself with&nbsp;
blame, still full of love and light,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:01.280
Haley tells him that it's okay. She&nbsp;
lets him go with a kiss and her ring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:06.000
promising to always love him. Whether the vision&nbsp;
was real or Hotch's coma-addled imagination,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.920
the scene provides beautiful closure for&nbsp;
her tragic — yet somehow hopeful — arc.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:16.640
LGBTQ+ relationships often meet tragic ends on&nbsp;
TV, but the one thing going for The Walking Dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:20.800
in this case, is the show's general propensity&nbsp;
to kill off pretty much everyone anyhow.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.080
Eric and Aaron were already dating when&nbsp;
the walkers began taking over — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:27.600
even the coming of the walking dead&nbsp;
couldn't tear them apart. Surprisingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.840
Eric's death isn't a result of the undead,&nbsp;
but a group of survivors called the Saviors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:36.000
Aaron pleads for him to keep going, making&nbsp;
it all that much more painful to watch.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.480
"You know I love you. You know i'm right."

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:45.680
Finally, realizing that his boyfriend's death&nbsp;
is inevitable, Aaron kisses Eric goodbye — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:49.920
fans are left to pick up the pieces of their&nbsp;
shattered hearts. Even worse, Aaron leaves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:54.000
Eric to die without killing him, allowing his&nbsp;
boyfriend to become a member of the undead.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.800
Most Doctor Who fans tend to prefer Rose&nbsp;
and the Tenth Doctor as a couple to Rose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:02.720
and the Ninth Doctor, but the fateful kiss&nbsp;
that causes Nine's regeneration into Ten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.040
is the spark that lights their love story —&nbsp;
and changes the course of the series forever.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.040
The writers made the bold but inevitable move&nbsp;
to kill off Nine, who was the first Doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:15.760
featured in the show's 2005 revival, once actor&nbsp;
Christopher Eccleston decided to leave the show.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:21.840
"It's a bit dodgy, this process. You&nbsp;
never know what you're gonna end up with."

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.440
And so, thanks to the creative differences&nbsp;
with Eccleston and the needs of an epic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:30.560
save-the-world story, the minute Rose and Nine&nbsp;
lock lips marks the end of Nine's existence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.920
All the compelling darkness and grief&nbsp;
that Christopher Eccleston had brought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:37.520
to the usually vivacious Doctor&nbsp;
was lost — after just one season.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:41.040
This sense of inevitability and&nbsp;
melancholy permeates the whole episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:46.240
making the final kiss between Rose and Nine both&nbsp;
cathartic and tragic. Sadly, it is, to date,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:50.560
the last time the Ninth Doctor has appeared on&nbsp;
screen outside of stock footage, as the drama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:56.080
between Eccleston and Doctor Who's producers&nbsp;
continued for years after he left the show.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:59.200
Buffy and Angel are the poster&nbsp;
children for tragic first love.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:06.800
"A vampire in love with a Slayer. It's&nbsp;
rather poetic, in a maudlin sort of way."

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:11.280
In simpler terms, their relationship is doomed&nbsp;
as all hell. Over the course of the show, Buffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:15.200
and Angel have seen their fair share of tragic&nbsp;
farewells — but none of their goodbyes are as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:20.400
cruel as the season 2 finale. Buffy ends up in a&nbsp;
battle for Angel's soul after their participation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:25.120
in a few minutes of "bad touch" gives Angel one&nbsp;
moment of happiness too many — causing him to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:30.320
transformed into the nefarious villain known as&nbsp;
Angelus. After going on a rampage, things get a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:35.680
little out of hand and Angelus opens a portal to&nbsp;
Hell. While Buffy succeeds in bringing back Angel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:40.160
it's too late by that point, and the only way&nbsp;
to close the portal is to chuck him right in.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:44.880
So, in tears, Buffy kisses her vampire lover&nbsp;
one more time before stabbing him as the portal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:49.920
sucks him in — and she loses her first love&nbsp;
forever. Well, not forever. But for a while.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:55.040
Michael and Sara just can't catch a break, as&nbsp;
they're always consistently torn apart whenever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:59.200
they find a moment to be happy. Given that the&nbsp;
show is called Prison Break, no one expected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:03.360
the innocent fugitive Michael to stay free for&nbsp;
long after escaping during the first season.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:08.000
So where did they go from there? Well, he ended&nbsp;
up in prison... again — and was forced to break&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:12.640
out... again. Yeah, it's a little convoluted,&nbsp;
but it is kinda the whole point of the show.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:16.080
When Michael's girlfriend Sara&nbsp;
kills a rogue FBI agent in Panama,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.000
she has a fairly understandable breakdown.&nbsp;
So Michael makes the impulsive decision to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:24.480
fake taking her hostage at gunpoint when they&nbsp;
get caught. They also both exchange verbal "I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:28.560
love you"s for the first time, sealing&nbsp;
the declaration with a desperate kiss.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:34.560
"You sacrificed everything for me once… No!&nbsp;
Don't move! Now it's time to say thank you."

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:39.760
As Sarah frantically protests, Michael takes the&nbsp;
blame for the killing and is subsequently arrested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:43.920
and imprisoned. The next season, the writers&nbsp;
wrote out a pregnant Sarah by shipping her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:49.200
character's decapitated head to Lincoln, a move&nbsp;
which wasn't exactly warmly-received by fans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:53.680
They later retconned that particular arc, after&nbsp;
those same fans demanded her return with e-mails&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:58.240
and boycotts — but it doesn't make Michael's&nbsp;
premature goodbye any less heartbreaking.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:02.000
Dealing with loss is hard enough&nbsp;
when it happens on one occasion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.400
but Grey's Anatomy likes to doll out death&nbsp;
blows like candy. In Izzie's case, after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:11.120
losing her love Denny once, she loses him all over&nbsp;
again when she herself is on the brink of death.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:16.320
Izzie initially watches Denny die when he suffers&nbsp;
from a stroke after a heart transplant surgery.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:20.960
Still, he lives on to haunt her in her mind —&nbsp;
which makes sense, as she cut his LVAD device&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:25.440
against his will to move him up the transplant&nbsp;
list, risking losing her medical license.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:29.360
When Izzie suffers from cancer symptoms, she&nbsp;
hallucinates Denny for a while — believing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:33.440
he's a ghost. As she kisses him one&nbsp;
last time, he disappears into thin air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:38.240
ripping them apart yet again, and leaving her&nbsp;
more lost and confused than ever. Fans will never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:42.320
quite know whether Denny was spiritually&nbsp;
there, or if it was just a hallucination.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:46.720
It's hard not to feel for Izzie, given all she's&nbsp;
been through, but the true tragedy lies with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:51.360
Denny and her refusal to let him go — which may be&nbsp;
the real reason she lost him in the first place.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:55.760
Game of Thrones easily wins the award&nbsp;
for forging more family connections&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:59.280
than any of its characters really ought&nbsp;
to have. And that's definitely the case&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:03.120
for Princess Myrcella, whose uncle,&nbsp;
Jaime Lannister, is also her father.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.040
Now, Game of Thrones fans meet many of&nbsp;
the series' deaths with ambivalence — or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:11.440
even celebration — but Princess Myrcella's&nbsp;
demise was nothing less than heartbreaking.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:15.680
Luckily — or unluckily — the princess'&nbsp;
mother, Cersei, is no stranger to revenge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:18.880
and in Myrcella's case, her&nbsp;
kiss of death happens twice.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:22.720
Because her mother is kind of the worst,&nbsp;
Myrcella is forced to flee Dorne and go back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:27.200
to King's Landing after her life is threatened.&nbsp;
Still hoping to avenge Prince Oberyn, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:31.920
the nefarious Ellaria Sand dons a fierce shade&nbsp;
of poisonous lipstick and kisses Myrcella before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:36.880
the young princess leaves. Only Ellaria has the&nbsp;
antidote, of course, and Myrcella is basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:41.520
doomed from the moment she leaves. Aboard the&nbsp;
ship home, Jaime, who is accompanying her home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:46.560
reveals that he's also her father. She admits&nbsp;
she's always had a hunch, accepting him anyway.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:51.520
Myrcella's nose begins to bleed, and it becomes&nbsp;
clear that something has gone very wrong indeed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:55.920
Jaime cradles Myrcella as she dies, and not&nbsp;
even the incestuous reveal is enough to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.920 --> 00:09:00.400
away the ironic Shakesperian tragedy of it&nbsp;
all. As one of the only genuinely innocent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:05.120
characters in the series, her brutal death&nbsp;
stands out as particularly cruel and unfair.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:07.360
Myrcella's death doesn't go unavenged, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:11.840
and Ellaria also gets her just desserts — in&nbsp;
the form of a poisonous kiss to her daughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:15.600
courtesy of Cersei. But hey,&nbsp;
that's life in Westeros , for you.

